# Microsoft Enterprise Error Handling Standards

## Enterprise Error Hierarchy

All errors extend [BaseError](mdc:src/domain/errors/base.error.ts) following **Microsoft enterprise patterns**:

```
BaseError (abstract) - Microsoft enterprise base
├── Service Errors (STTError, LLMError, TTSError, etc.) - Enterprise service layer
├── Validation Errors (ValidationError, FileValidationError) - Enterprise validation
├── External API Errors (OpenAIAPIError, TelegramAPIError) - Enterprise API integration
└── Resource Errors (NotFoundError, AlreadyExistsError) - Enterprise resource management
```

## Usage Pattern

```typescript
try {
  const result = await operation();
  return result;
} catch (error) {
  logger.error('Operation failed', {
    error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),
    context: {
      /* relevant data */
    },
  });
  throw new ServiceError('User-friendly message', {
    /* context */
  });
}
```

## Error Handler

Use [ErrorHandler](mdc:src/domain/errors/index.ts) in middleware:

```typescript
const message = ErrorHandler.handle(error); // User-friendly message
const isRecoverable = ErrorHandler.isRecoverable(error);
const retryDelay = ErrorHandler.getRetryDelay(error);
```

## Creating Errors

```typescript
throw new STTError('Transcription failed', {
  audioPath,
  fileSize,
  originalError: error.message,
});
```

## Rules

- ✅ Always use typed errors (not generic Error)
- ✅ Include context in error objects
- ✅ Log errors with full context before throwing
- ✅ Return user-friendly messages via getUserMessage()
- ❌ Never expose sensitive data in error messages
